const TermsOfService = "<h1>TERMS OF SERVICE</h1>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<p>We are T1DNZ ('Company', 'Owner', 'we', 'us', or 'our').</p>\n<p>We operate Nighttroop, a web service that stores diabetes data and shares it with the people, devices and apps you choose (the 'Service'), as well as any other related products and services that refer or link to these legal terms (the 'Legal Terms') (collectively, the 'Services'). We refer to you, and any other person who you use the app on behalf of, as a &quot;User&quot;.</p>\n<p>You can contact us by email at <strong><a href=\"mailto:SUPPORT_EMAIL\">SUPPORT_EMAIL</a></strong></p>\n<p>These Legal Terms constitute a legally binding agreement made between you, whether personally or on behalf of an entity ('you'), and T1DNZ, concerning your access to and use of the Services. You agree that by accessing the Services, you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by all of these Legal Terms. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE WITH ALL OF THESE LEGAL TERMS, THEN YOU ARE EXPRESSLY PROHIBITED FROM USING THE SERVICES AND YOU MUST DISCONTINUE USE IMMEDIATELY.</p>\n<p>Supplemental terms and conditions or documents that may be posted on the Services from time to time are hereby expressly incorporated herein by reference. We reserve the right, in our sole discretion, to make changes or modifications to these Legal Terms from time to time. We will alert you about any changes by updating the 'Last updated' date of these Legal Terms, and you waive any right to receive specific notice of each such change. It is your responsibility to periodically review these Legal Terms to stay informed of updates. You will be subject to, and will be deemed to have been made aware of and to have accepted, the changes in any revised Legal Terms by your continued use of the Services after the date such revised Legal Terms are posted.</p>\n<h2>1. IT IS NOT A MEDICAL OR HEALTHCARE SERVICE</h2>\n<p>1.1 Services are not medical or healthcare services. You understand that T1DNZ is not a healthcare professional and does not provide medical, health or other professional services or advice, nor do we verify the accuracy of User Data. Services and Software Apps are not replacements for proper medical care, and you agree that the User is solely responsible for obtaining proper treatment for his or her conditions. You may provide the information and reports received from Services to the User's healthcare providers at your own responsibility, understanding that the Services are provided without warranty except as required by law or as otherwise expressly set forth in this Agreement.</p>\n<p>1.2 The information provided when using the Services is not intended for distribution to or use by any person or entity in any jurisdiction or country where such distribution or use would be contrary to law or regulation or which would subject us to any registration requirement within such jurisdiction or country. Accordingly, those persons who choose to access the Services from other locations do so on their own initiative and are solely responsible for compliance with local laws, if and to the extent local laws are applicable. The Services are not tailored to comply with industry-specific regulations (Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) etc.), so if your interactions would be subjected to such laws, you may not use the Services.</p>\n<p>1.3 By using the Services, you represent and warrant that: (1) you have the legal capacity and you agree to comply with these Legal Terms; (2) you are not a minor in the jurisdiction in which you reside; (3) you will not access the Services through automated or non-human means, whether through a bot, script or otherwise, except through the interfaces the Services provide for devices and apps, such as uploaders and Nightscout compatible apps; (4) you will not use the Services for any illegal or unauthorised purpose; and (5) your use of the Services will not violate any applicable law or regulation.</p>\n<p>1.4 Our Services are intended to allow a User to use the data fetched from, or created by, other services to help the User manage his or her diabetes. Use of our Services requires an internet-enabled Smart Device or computer. Each Service receives Data from other services that is stored. Our Services process Data applying methodologies, provide data, and where applicable, provide reports, to Users. Our Services may also permit Users to share User Data, reports and other information relating to the User. You acknowledge and agree that Services are not a substitute for regular monitoring and medical care, and that you will ensure that all appropriate treatment, attention and efforts are made by and for the benefit of the User, as applicable, to maintain his or her health and wellness. Our collection, storage and transmission of User Data and any other information that you provide to through Services and Software Apps is governed by the Privacy Policy.</p>\n<p>1.5 Alarms and other notifications from the Services may be late, wrong or not delivered at all, for example when a device, an app, a network or the Services are not working. They must not be relied on to keep the User safe, and are not a replacement for a medical device's own alarms.</p>\n<p>1.6 The Services can fetch Data from other services you choose to connect, such as Dexcom, LibreLinkUp or a Nightscout site. You confirm that you have the right to connect them and to share their Data with the Services. Your use of those services is governed by their own terms, and we are not responsible for them, their Data or their availability.</p>\n<h2>2. PRIVACY POLICY</h2>\n<p>2.1 We care about data privacy and security. Please review our Privacy Policy. By using the Services, you agree to be bound by our Privacy Policy.</p>\n<p>2.2. Please be advised the Services may be hosted in another country from the User's location or residence. If you access the Services from any other region of the world with laws or other requirements governing personal data collection, use, or disclosure that differ from applicable laws of the country the Services are hosted in, then through your continued use of the Services, and you expressly consent to have your data transferred to and processed in the country where the Services are hosted.</p>\n<p>2.3 You and Services agree that we may access, store, process, and use any information and personal data that you provide following the terms of the Privacy Policy and your choices (including settings). By sending Data to the Services, whether you enter it, upload it from a device or app, or set up a sync that fetches it, you consent to us storing and processing it to provide the Services, as the Privacy Policy describes. By submitting suggestions or other feedback regarding the Services, you agree that we can use and share such feedback for any purpose without compensation to you.</p>\n<h2>3. SERVICES MANAGEMENT</h2>\n<p>3.1 We reserve the right, but not the obligation, to: (1) monitor the Services for violations of these Legal Terms; (2) take appropriate legal action against anyone who, in our sole discretion, violates the law or these Legal Terms, including without limitation, reporting such user to law enforcement authorities; (3) in our sole discretion and without limitation, refuse, restrict access to, limit the availability of, or disable (to the extent technologically feasible) any of your Contributions or any portion thereof; (4) in our sole discretion and without limitation, notice, or liability, to remove from the Services or otherwise disable all files and content that are excessive in size or are in any way burdensome to our systems; and (5) otherwise manage the Services in a manner designed to protect our rights and property and to facilitate the proper functioning of the Services.</p>\n<h2>4. LIABILITY</h2>\n<p>4.1 We are not responsible for third-party matters. Without limiting the provisions of this Agreement or expanding the scope of our responsibilities, T1DNZ is not responsible for outages or defects in power, telecommunications, computers, Smart Devices, third party software and any other event outside of our  direct control.</p>\n<p>4.2 In no event will T1DNZ be liable to you or any third party for any direct, indirect, consequential, exemplary, incidental, special, or punitive damages, including lost profit, lost revenue, loss of data, or other damages arising from your use of the Services, even if we have been advised of the possibility of such damages.</p>\n<h2>5. TERM AND TERMINATION</h2>\n<p>5.1 These Legal Terms shall remain in full force and effect while you use the Services. You may stop using the Services at any time, and a site's admin can delete the site from its settings. Without limiting any other provision of these legal terms, we reserve the right to, in our sole discretion and without notice or liability, deny access to and use of the Services (including blocking certain ip addresses), to any person for any reason or for no reason, including without limitation for breach of any representation, warranty, or covenant contained in these legal terms or of any applicable law or regulation. We may terminate your use or participation in the Services or delete any content or information that you posted at any time, without warning, in our sole discretion.</p>\n<p>5.2 If we terminate or suspend your account for any reason, you are prohibited from registering and creating a new account, even if you may be acting on behalf of the third party. In addition to terminating or suspending your account, we reserve the right to take appropriate legal action, including without limitation pursuing civil, criminal, and injunctive redress.</p>\n<h2>6. MODIFICATIONS AND INTERRUPTIONS</h2>\n<p>6.1 We reserve the right to change, modify, or remove the contents of the Services at any time or for any reason at our sole discretion without notice. However, we have no obligation to update any information on our Services.</p>\n<p>6.2 We will not be liable to you or any third party for any modification, price change, suspension, or discontinuance of the Services.</p>\n<p>6.3 We cannot guarantee the Services will be available at all times. We may experience hardware, software, or other problems or need to perform maintenance related to the Services, resulting in interruptions, delays, or errors. We reserve the right to change, revise, update, suspend, discontinue, or otherwise modify the Services at any time or for any reason without notice to you. You agree that we have no liability whatsoever for any loss, damage, or inconvenience caused by your inability to access or use the Services during any downtime or discontinuance of the Services. Nothing in these Legal Terms will be construed to obligate us to maintain and support the Services or to supply any corrections, updates, or releases in connection therewith.</p>\n<h2>7. DISPUTE RESOLUTION</h2>\n<p>7.1 These Legal Terms shall be governed by and defined following the laws of New Zealand. T1DNZ and yourself irrevocably consent that the courts of New Zealand shall have exclusive jurisdiction to resolve any dispute which may arise in connection with these Legal Terms.</p>\n<p>7.2 Informal Negotiations: To expedite resolution and control the cost of any dispute, controversy, or claim related to these Legal Terms (each a 'Dispute' and collectively, the 'Disputes') brought by either you or us (individually, a 'Party' and collectively, the 'Parties'), the Parties agree to first attempt to negotiate any Dispute (except those Disputes expressly provided below) informally for at least thirty (30) days before initiating arbitration. Such informal negotiations commence upon written notice from one Party to the other Party.</p>\n<p>7.3 Arbitration: Any dispute arising out of or in connection with these Legal Terms, including any question regarding its existence, validity, or termination, shall be referred to and resolved by arbitration according to the New Zealand Arbitration Act 1996, which, as a result of referring to it, is considered as the part of this clause. The number of arbitrators shall be two (2). The seat, or legal place, or arbitration shall be Wellington, New Zealand.</p>\n<p>7.4 The language of the proceedings shall be English. The governing law of these Legal Terms shall be substantive law of New Zealand.</p>\n<p>7.5 Restrictions The Parties agree that any arbitration shall be limited to the Dispute between the Parties individually. To the full extent permitted by law, (a) no arbitration shall be joined with any other proceeding; (b) there is no right or authority for any Dispute to be arbitrated on a class-action basis or to utilise class action procedures; and (c) there is no right or authority for any Dispute to be brought in a purported representative capacity on behalf of the general public or any other persons.</p>\n<p>7.6 Exceptions to Informal Negotiations and Arbitration The Parties agree that the following Disputes are not subject to the above provisions concerning informal negotiations arbitration: (a) any Disputes seeking to enforce or protect, or concerning the validity of, any of the intellectual property rights of a Party; (b) any Dispute related to, or arising from, allegations of theft, piracy, invasion of privacy, or unauthorised use; and (c) any claim for injunctive relief. If this provision is found to be illegal or unenforceable, then neither Party will elect to arbitrate any Dispute falling within that portion of this provision found to be illegal or unenforceable and such Dispute shall be decided by a court of competent jurisdiction within the courts listed for jurisdiction above, and the Parties agree to submit to the personal jurisdiction of that court.</p>\n<h2>8. CORRECTIONS</h2>\n<p>8.1 There may be information on the Services that contains typographical errors, inaccuracies, or omissions, including descriptions, pricing, availability, and various other information. We reserve the right to correct any errors, inaccuracies, or omissions and to change or update the information on the Services at any time, without prior notice.</p>\n<h2>9. DISCLAIMER</h2>\n<p>9.1 The Services are provided on an as-is and as-available basis. You agree that your use of the Services will be at your sole risk. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, in connection with the Services and your use thereof, including, without limitation, the implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.</p>\n<p>9.2 We make no warranties or representations about the accuracy or completeness of the Services content or the content of any websites or mobile applications linked to the Services and we will assume no liability or responsibility for any (1) errors, mistakes, or inaccuracies of content and materials, (2) personal injury or property damage, of any nature whatsoever, resulting from your access to and use of the Services, (3) any unauthorised access to or use of our secure servers and/or any and all personal information and/or financial information stored therein, (4) any interruption or cessation of transmission to or from the Services, (5) any bugs, viruses, trojan horses, or the like which may be transmitted to or through the Services by any third party, and/or (6) any errors or omissions in any content and materials or for any loss or damage of any kind incurred as a result of the use of any content posted, transmitted, or otherwise made available via the Services.</p>\n<p>9.3 We do not warrant, endorse, guarantee, or assume responsibility for any product or service advertised or offered by a third party through the Services, any hyperlinked website, or any website or mobile application featured in any banner or other advertising, and we will not be a party to or in any way be responsible for monitoring any transaction between you and any third-party providers of products or Services. As with the purchase of a product or service through any medium or in any environment, you should use your best judgement and exercise caution where appropriate.</p>\n<h2>10. INDEMNIFICATION</h2>\n<p>10.1 You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold us harmless, including our subsidiaries, affiliates, and all of our respective officers, agents, partners, and employees, from and against any loss, damage, liability, claim, or demand, including reasonable attorneys’ fees and expenses, made by any third party due to or arising out of: (1) use of the Services; (2) breach of these Legal Terms; (3) any breach of your representations and warranties set forth in these Legal Terms; (4) your violation of the rights of a third party, including but not limited to intellectual property rights; or (5) any overt harmful act toward any other user of the Services with whom you connected via the Services. Notwithstanding the foregoing, we reserve the right, at your expense, to assume the exclusive defence and control of any matter for which you are required to indemnify us, and you agree to cooperate, at your expense, with our defence of such claims. We will use reasonable efforts to notify you of any such claim, action, or proceeding which is subject to this indemnification upon becoming aware of it.</p>\n<h2>11. USER DATA</h2>\n<p>11.1 We will maintain certain data that you transmit to the Services for the purpose of managing the performance of the Services, as well as data relating to your use of the Services. Although we perform regular routine backups of data, you are solely responsible for all data that you transmit or that relates to any activity you have undertaken using the Services. You agree that we shall have no liability to you for any loss or corruption of any such data, and you hereby waive any right of action against us arising from any such loss or corruption of such data. A site's admin can download a copy of the site's data from its settings at any time.</p>\n<h2>12. ELECTRONIC COMMUNICATIONS, TRANSACTIONS, AND SIGNATURES</h2>\n<p>12.1 Visiting the Services, sending us emails, and completing online forms constitute electronic communications. You consent to receive electronic communications, and you agree that all agreements, notices, disclosures, and other communications we provide to you electronically, via email and on the Services, satisfy any legal requirement that such communication be in writing.</p>\n<p>12.2 You hereby agree to the use of electronic signatures, contracts, orders, and other records, and to electronic delivery of notices, policies, and records of transactions initiated or completed by us or via the Services.</p>\n<p>12.3 You hereby waive any rights or requirements under any statutes, regulations, rules, ordinances, or other laws in any jurisdiction which require an original signature or delivery or retention of non-electronic records, or to payments or the granting of credits by any means other than electronic means.</p>\n<h2>13. MISCELLANEOUS</h2>\n<p>13.1 These Legal Terms and any policies or operating rules posted by us on the Services or in respect to the Services constitute the entire agreement and understanding between you and us. Our failure to exercise or enforce any right or provision of these Legal Terms shall not operate as a waiver of such right or provision. These Legal Terms operate to the fullest extent permissible by law. We may assign any or all of our rights and obligations to others at any time. We shall not be responsible or liable for any loss, damage, delay, or failure to act caused by any cause beyond our reasonable control. If any provision or part of a provision of these Legal Terms is determined to be unlawful, void, or unenforceable, that provision or part of the provision is deemed severable from these Legal Terms and does not affect the validity and enforceability of any remaining provisions. There is no joint venture, partnership, employment or agency relationship created between you and us as a result of these Legal Terms or use of the Services. You agree that these Legal Terms will not be construed against us by virtue of having drafted them. You hereby waive any and all defences you may have based on the electronic form of these Legal Terms and the lack of signing by the parties hereto to execute these Legal Terms.</p>\n<h2>14. CONTACT US</h2>\n<p>In order to resolve a complaint regarding the Services or to receive further information regarding use of the Services, please contact us at:\nT1DNZ <strong><a href=\"mailto:SUPPORT_EMAIL\">SUPPORT_EMAIL</a></strong></p>\n<h2>Version</h2>\n<p>Last Changed - 2026-10-30</p>\n"

// PrivacyPolicy is PRIVACY_POLICY.md as HTML
const PrivacyPolicy = "<h1>PRIVACY POLICY</h1>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<p>This privacy policy explains what Data Nighttroop (the 'Service'), operated by T1DNZ (the 'Owner'), keeps about its Users, why, and what Users can do about it. To ask about your Personal Data, the purposes it is used for and the parties it is shared with, contact the Owner.</p>\n<p>Owner contact email: <strong><a href=\"mailto:SUPPORT_EMAIL\">SUPPORT_EMAIL</a></strong></p>\n<h2>Consent by Sending Data</h2>\n<p>The Service is a web service that stores and processes data, so that Users and the people and devices they choose can see it. By sending Data to the Service, whether you enter it on a site, upload it from a device or app, or set up a sync that fetches it from another service, you consent to the Owner storing and processing that Data to provide the Service, as this policy describes. If you send Data about another person, such as someone you care for, you confirm that you have their consent, or are legally able to give it for them.</p>\n<p>You can withdraw this consent at any time by no longer sending Data and deleting your site, as described under The Rights of Users.</p>\n<h2>Types of Data collected</h2>\n<p>The Service keeps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>User Data</strong> that is sent to a site: such as glucose readings, insulin doses, food, temporary targets and basal rates, profiles, devices and their status, notes, and the settings and alarms of the site and its Users. This User Data is sensitive, and is only used to provide the Service.</li>\n<li><strong>Account Data</strong>: such as each site's address, and the names, roles, settings and sign-in details of the Users and devices of a site. Passwords are stored only as hashes.</li>\n<li><strong>Sync credentials</strong>: such as the usernames, passwords, addresses and tokens of other services (such as Dexcom, LibreLinkUp and Nightscout) a site is set up to sync from. These are encrypted when stored, and are only used to fetch the site's Data.</li>\n<li><strong>Usage Data</strong>: such as logs of requests to the Service, including IP addresses, the times of requests and what was requested, and records of the Service's own jobs and errors, such as syncs and backups.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The Service uses one cookie, to keep a User signed in. It does not use advertising or analytics tracking.</p>\n<p>Unless the Service says otherwise, Data it asks for is needed to provide the Service, and leaving it out may stop the Service working.</p>\n<h2>Methods of Processing</h2>\n<p>The Owner takes appropriate security measures to prevent unauthorised access, disclosure, modification or destruction of the Data, including encrypting credentials and backups. The Data is processed by computers, following procedures strictly related to the purposes in this policy.</p>\n<p>A site's Data is shown only to the Users and devices of that site, and to anyone they give its address and a token or password to, such as Nightscout apps. It is not shown to other sites.</p>\n<p>Besides the Owner, the Data may be accessible to people involved in running the Service (administration, legal, system administration) and to third-party technical service providers, such as hosting, backup storage and error reporting services, appointed by the Owner as Data Processors where needed.</p>\n<h2>Legal Basis of Processing</h2>\n<p>The Owner may process Personal Data relating to Users if one of the following applies:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Users have given their consent for one or more specific purposes, including by sending Data to the Service, as described above.</li>\n<li>Provision of Data is necessary for the performance of an agreement with the User and/or for any pre-contractual obligations thereof.</li>\n<li>Processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which the Owner is subject.</li>\n<li>Processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Owner or by a third party, such as keeping the Service secure and running.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Place</h2>\n<p>The Data is processed where the Service and its providers are hosted, and where the parties involved in the processing are located.</p>\n<p>Depending on the User's location, this may involve transferring the User's Data to a country other than their own.</p>\n<h2>Retention Time</h2>\n<p>Personal Data is stored for as long as needed for the purpose it was collected for:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>A site's Data is kept while the site is in use. A site that is not used for a long time may be disabled, and later archived: its Data is removed from the Service and kept only in an encrypted archive, so it can be restored. A site that was never used may be deleted.</li>\n<li>Usage Data is kept for as long as needed to run, secure and fix the Service, and is then removed.</li>\n<li>Encrypted backups of the Service are kept for a limited time, so that it can be restored after a failure.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The Owner may keep Personal Data for longer when required to by a legal obligation or by order of an authority.</p>\n<p>Once the retention period expires, Personal Data is deleted, and the right to access, erasure, rectification and data portability can no longer be enforced.</p>\n<h2>The Rights of Users</h2>\n<p>Users may exercise certain rights over their Data processed by the Owner. In particular, Users have the right to:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Withdraw their consent at any time</strong>: by no longer sending Data to the Service, and deleting their site.</li>\n<li><strong>Object to processing of their Data</strong>: where the processing is carried out on a legal basis other than consent.</li>\n<li><strong>Access their Data</strong>: a site's admin can see all its Data on the site, and download a copy of it.</li>\n<li><strong>Verify and seek rectification</strong>: Users can correct their Data on the site, or ask the Owner to.</li>\n<li><strong>Restrict the processing of their Data</strong>: under certain circumstances; the Owner will then only store the Data.</li>\n<li><strong>Have their Data deleted</strong>: a site's admin can delete the site, which removes it from the Service and keeps it only in an encrypted archive for a limited time. To have the archive erased too, contact the Owner.</li>\n<li><strong>Receive their Data and have it transferred to another controller</strong>: the site's Data can be downloaded in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format, and much of it is also available through the Service's Nightscout compatible API.</li>\n<li><strong>Lodge a complaint</strong>: with their competent data protection authority, such as the New Zealand Privacy Commissioner.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>How to exercise these rights</h2>\n<p>Requests to exercise User rights can be sent to the Owner at the contact email in this document. They are free of charge, and will be answered as early as possible.</p>\n<h2>Legal action</h2>\n<p>The User's Personal Data may be used for legal purposes by the Owner in Court, or in the stages leading to possible legal action, arising from improper use of the Service.\nThe User is aware that the Owner may be required to reveal Personal Data upon request of public authorities.</p>\n<h2>System logs and maintenance</h2>\n<p>To run and maintain the Service, the Service and its third-party providers keep logs of interactions with the Service, which may include Personal Data such as IP addresses.</p>\n<h2>Information not contained in this policy</h2>\n<p>More details about the collection or processing of Personal Data may be requested from the Owner at any time, at the contact email in this document.</p>\n<h2>Changes to this privacy policy</h2>\n<p>The Owner may change this privacy policy at any time, giving notice to Users on this page. It is recommended to check this page often.</p>\n<p>Should the changes affect processing based on the User's consent, the Owner will collect new consent from the User, where required.</p>\n<p>Owner contact email: <strong><a href=\"mailto:SUPPORT_EMAIL\">SUPPORT_EMAIL</a></strong></p>\n<h2>Version</h2>\n<p>Last Changed - 2026-10-30</p>\n"

// APIDocs is clients/nighttroop/openapi.json as HTML
const APIDocs = "<h1>Nighttroop API <small>0.1.0</small></h1>\n<p>Nighttroop's JSON API. POST /site is on the public host (<code>https://&lt;host&gt;</code>); /api/... is the Nightscout API, on a site's Nightscout host (<code>https://&lt;site&gt;.ns.&lt;host&gt;</code>); everything else is on a site's host (<code>https://&lt;site&gt;.&lt;host&gt;</code>) with a JWT from POST /login. Times are milliseconds since the epoch, and glucose is in the units of the signed in identity's settings; a Nightscout document says its units in its units field.</p>\n\n<p><a id=\"api-docs--download\" href=\"/openapi.json\" download=\"openapi.json\">Download the OpenAPI schema</a></p>\n<h2>Endpoints</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Count\"><code>GET /api/v1/count/{collection}/where</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Echo\"><code>GET /api/v1/echo/{collection}</code></a> How a search of the collection is understood, without running it</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1ExperimentsTest\"><code>GET /api/v1/experiments/test</code></a> How Loop checks its API secret: 200 when it can upload treatments</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Slice\"><code>GET /api/v1/slice/{collection}/{field}/{type}/{prefix}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Status\"><code>GET /api/v1/status</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Times\"><code>GET /api/v1/times/{prefix}</code></a> The entries whose dateString starts with the prefix, such as 2026-10</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1VerifyAuth\"><code>GET /api/v1/verifyauth</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Versions\"><code>GET /api/v1/versions</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Search\"><code>GET /api/v1/{collection}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Create\"><code>POST /api/v1/{collection}</code></a> Creates one document or each in an array, and returns those created</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1ReplaceByBody\"><code>PUT /api/v1/{collection}</code></a> Replaces the document with the _id in the body</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1DeleteByQuery\"><code>DELETE /api/v1/{collection}</code></a> Soft deletes the entries a search with the query finds, at most 1000, as xDrip4iOS deletes readings; only entries, and any other filter or one without a date is a 400</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Current\"><code>GET /api/v1/{collection}/current</code></a> The newest document, in a list of one; for profile, as in Nightscout, the profile set itself</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Get\"><code>GET /api/v1/{collection}/{identifier}</code></a> The document with the identifier, or the documents of a type, such as sgv</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Replace\"><code>PUT /api/v1/{collection}/{identifier}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV1Delete\"><code>DELETE /api/v1/{collection}/{identifier}</code></a> Deletes the document with the identifier, or the documents of a type</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV2CheckPermission\"><code>GET /api/v2/authorization/debug/check/{permission}</code></a> Whether the token or JWT has a permission, such as api:settings:create: 200 when it has, 403 when not</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV2Authorize\"><code>GET /api/v2/authorization/request/{token}</code></a> Exchanges a device&#39;s Nightscout token for a JWT</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV2Properties\"><code>GET /api/v2/properties</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV2PropertiesNamed\"><code>GET /api/v2/properties/{names}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV2Summary\"><code>GET /api/v2/summary</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Authorize\"><code>GET /api/v3/authorization/request/{token}</code></a> Exchanges a device&#39;s Nightscout token for a JWT</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3LastModified\"><code>GET /api/v3/lastModified</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Status\"><code>GET /api/v3/status</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Test\"><code>GET /api/v3/test</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Version\"><code>GET /api/v3/version</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Search\"><code>GET /api/v3/{collection}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Create\"><code>POST /api/v3/{collection}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3History\"><code>GET /api/v3/{collection}/history/{since}</code></a> The documents changed since a time, the oldest change first, including deletions</li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Read\"><code>GET /api/v3/{collection}/{identifier}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Replace\"><code>PUT /api/v3/{collection}/{identifier}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Patch\"><code>PATCH /api/v3/{collection}/{identifier}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#NsV3Delete\"><code>DELETE /api/v3/{collection}/{identifier}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#ListFoodIntakes\"><code>GET /data/food</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#CreateFoodIntake\"><code>POST /data/food</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#GetFoodIntake\"><code>GET /data/food/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#UpdateFoodIntake\"><code>POST /data/food/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#DeleteFoodIntake\"><code>DELETE /data/food/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#ListGlucoseReadings\"><code>GET /data/glucose</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#CreateGlucoseReading\"><code>POST /data/glucose</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#GetGlucoseReading\"><code>GET /data/glucose/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#UpdateGlucoseReading\"><code>POST /data/glucose/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#DeleteGlucoseReading\"><code>DELETE /data/glucose/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#ListInsulinDoses\"><code>GET /data/insulin</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#CreateInsulinDose\"><code>POST /data/insulin</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#GetInsulinDose\"><code>GET /data/insulin/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#UpdateInsulinDose\"><code>POST /data/insulin/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#DeleteInsulinDose\"><code>DELETE /data/insulin/{id}</code></a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"#Login\"><code>POST /login</code></a> Signs an admin (with TOTP) or user in, for a JWT</li>\n<li><a href=\"#CreateSite\"><code>POST /site</code></a> Creates a site, on the public host, and gives its credentials once</li>\n<li><a href=\"#GetSummary\"><code>GET /summary</code></a> The site&#39;s summary over the last hours (48 by default, a week at most)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<section id=\"NsV1Count\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/count/{collection}/where</code></h2>\n<p>NsV1Count</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>date$gte</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Documents from this time, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>date$lte</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Documents up to this time, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Echo\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/echo/{collection}</code></h2>\n<p>How a search of the collection is understood, without running it</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1ExperimentsTest\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/experiments/test</code></h2>\n<p>How Loop checks its API secret: 200 when it can upload treatments</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Slice\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/slice/{collection}/{field}/{type}/{prefix}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV1Slice</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>field</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>type</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>prefix</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>count</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>How many documents, at most 1000</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Status\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/status</code></h2>\n<p>NsV1Status</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Times\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/times/{prefix}</code></h2>\n<p>The entries whose dateString starts with the prefix, such as 2026-10</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>prefix</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>count</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>How many documents, at most 1000</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1VerifyAuth\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/verifyauth</code></h2>\n<p>NsV1VerifyAuth</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Versions\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/versions</code></h2>\n<p>NsV1Versions</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Search\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/{collection}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV1Search</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>count</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>How many documents, at most 1000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>skip</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>sort</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>A field to sort by, ascending</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>sort$desc</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>A field to sort by, descending</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>fields</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>Comma separated fields to return</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>date$gte</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Documents from this time, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>date$lte</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Documents up to this time, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Create\">\n<h2><code>POST /api/v1/{collection}</code></h2>\n<p>Creates one document or each in an array, and returns those created</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1ReplaceByBody\">\n<h2><code>PUT /api/v1/{collection}</code></h2>\n<p>Replaces the document with the _id in the body</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1DeleteByQuery\">\n<h2><code>DELETE /api/v1/{collection}</code></h2>\n<p>Soft deletes the entries a search with the query finds, at most 1000, as xDrip4iOS deletes readings; only entries, and any other filter or one without a date is a 400</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>find[type]</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>Documents of this type, such as sgv</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>find[date][$gte]</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Documents from this time, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>find[date][$lte]</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Documents up to this time, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>find[date][$in][]</code></td><td>query</td><td>array of integer (int64)</td><td>Documents at exactly these times, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Current\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/{collection}/current</code></h2>\n<p>The newest document, in a list of one; for profile, as in Nightscout, the profile set itself</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Get\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v1/{collection}/{identifier}</code></h2>\n<p>The document with the identifier, or the documents of a type, such as sgv</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>identifier</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>count</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>How many documents, at most 1000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>fields</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>Comma separated fields to return</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Replace\">\n<h2><code>PUT /api/v1/{collection}/{identifier}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV1Replace</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>identifier</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV1Delete\">\n<h2><code>DELETE /api/v1/{collection}/{identifier}</code></h2>\n<p>Deletes the document with the identifier, or the documents of a type</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>identifier</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>permanent</code></td><td>query</td><td>boolean</td><td>Deletes the row instead of marking it deleted</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV2CheckPermission\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v2/authorization/debug/check/{permission}</code></h2>\n<p>Whether the token or JWT has a permission, such as api:settings:create: 200 when it has, 403 when not</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>permission</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV2Authorize\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v2/authorization/request/{token}</code></h2>\n<p>Exchanges a device&#39;s Nightscout token for a JWT</p>\n\n<p>No sign in needed</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>token</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A JWT</td><td><a href=\"#schema-NsAuthorization\">NsAuthorization</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV2Properties\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v2/properties</code></h2>\n<p>NsV2Properties</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV2PropertiesNamed\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v2/properties/{names}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV2PropertiesNamed</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>names</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td>Comma separated, such as bgnow,delta</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV2Summary\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v2/summary</code></h2>\n<p>NsV2Summary</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Authorize\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v3/authorization/request/{token}</code></h2>\n<p>Exchanges a device&#39;s Nightscout token for a JWT</p>\n\n<p>No sign in needed</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>token</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A JWT</td><td><a href=\"#schema-NsAuthorization\">NsAuthorization</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3LastModified\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v3/lastModified</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3LastModified</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>An API v3 result</td><td>{result: , status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Status\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v3/status</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Status</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>An API v3 result</td><td>{result: , status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Test\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v3/test</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Test</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>An API v3 result</td><td>{result: , status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Version\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v3/version</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Version</p>\n\n<p>No sign in needed</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>An API v3 result</td><td>{result: , status: integer}</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Search\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v3/{collection}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Search</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>At most 1000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>skip</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>sort</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>A field to sort by, ascending</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>sort$desc</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>A field to sort by, descending</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>fields</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>Comma separated fields to return</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>date$gte</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Documents from this time, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>date$lte</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Documents up to this time, in milliseconds</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Documents</td><td>{result: array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Create\">\n<h2><code>POST /api/v3/{collection}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Create</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A document</td><td>{identifier: string, isDeduplication: boolean, lastModified: integer (int64), result: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>201</td><td>A document</td><td>{identifier: string, isDeduplication: boolean, lastModified: integer (int64), result: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3History\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v3/{collection}/history/{since}</code></h2>\n<p>The documents changed since a time, the oldest change first, including deletions</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>since</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>At most 1000</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Documents</td><td>{result: array of <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Read\">\n<h2><code>GET /api/v3/{collection}/{identifier}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Read</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>identifier</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>fields</code></td><td>query</td><td>string</td><td>Comma separated fields to return</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A document</td><td>{identifier: string, isDeduplication: boolean, lastModified: integer (int64), result: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Replace\">\n<h2><code>PUT /api/v3/{collection}/{identifier}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Replace</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>identifier</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A document</td><td>{identifier: string, isDeduplication: boolean, lastModified: integer (int64), result: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>201</td><td>A document</td><td>{identifier: string, isDeduplication: boolean, lastModified: integer (int64), result: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Patch\">\n<h2><code>PATCH /api/v3/{collection}/{identifier}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Patch</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>identifier</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A document</td><td>{identifier: string, isDeduplication: boolean, lastModified: integer (int64), result: <a href=\"#schema-NsDocument\">NsDocument</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"NsV3Delete\">\n<h2><code>DELETE /api/v3/{collection}/{identifier}</code></h2>\n<p>NsV3Delete</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer, or a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the token query, or the SHA-1 hex of a device&#39;s Nightscout token, as the api-secret header</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>collection</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string, one of entries, treatments, devicestatus, profile, food, settings, activity</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>identifier</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>permanent</code></td><td>query</td><td>boolean</td><td>Deletes the row instead of marking it deleted</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A Nightscout response</td><td>object</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>A Nightscout error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"ListFoodIntakes\">\n<h2><code>GET /data/food</code></h2>\n<p>ListFoodIntakes</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>At most 1000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>skip</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Food intakes, newest first</td><td>{result: array of <a href=\"#schema-FoodIntake\">FoodIntake</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"CreateFoodIntake\">\n<h2><code>POST /data/food</code></h2>\n<p>CreateFoodIntake</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-FoodIntake\">FoodIntake</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>201</td><td>A food intake</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-FoodIntake\">FoodIntake</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"GetFoodIntake\">\n<h2><code>GET /data/food/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>GetFoodIntake</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A food intake</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-FoodIntake\">FoodIntake</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"UpdateFoodIntake\">\n<h2><code>POST /data/food/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>UpdateFoodIntake</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-FoodIntake\">FoodIntake</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A food intake</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-FoodIntake\">FoodIntake</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"DeleteFoodIntake\">\n<h2><code>DELETE /data/food/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>DeleteFoodIntake</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Deleted</td><td>{status: string}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"ListGlucoseReadings\">\n<h2><code>GET /data/glucose</code></h2>\n<p>ListGlucoseReadings</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>At most 1000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>skip</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Readings, newest first</td><td>{result: array of <a href=\"#schema-GlucoseReading\">GlucoseReading</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"CreateGlucoseReading\">\n<h2><code>POST /data/glucose</code></h2>\n<p>CreateGlucoseReading</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-GlucoseReading\">GlucoseReading</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>201</td><td>A reading</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-GlucoseReading\">GlucoseReading</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"GetGlucoseReading\">\n<h2><code>GET /data/glucose/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>GetGlucoseReading</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A reading</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-GlucoseReading\">GlucoseReading</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"UpdateGlucoseReading\">\n<h2><code>POST /data/glucose/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>UpdateGlucoseReading</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-GlucoseReading\">GlucoseReading</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A reading</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-GlucoseReading\">GlucoseReading</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"DeleteGlucoseReading\">\n<h2><code>DELETE /data/glucose/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>DeleteGlucoseReading</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Deleted</td><td>{status: string}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"ListInsulinDoses\">\n<h2><code>GET /data/insulin</code></h2>\n<p>ListInsulinDoses</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>At most 1000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>skip</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Doses, newest first</td><td>{result: array of <a href=\"#schema-InsulinDose\">InsulinDose</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"CreateInsulinDose\">\n<h2><code>POST /data/insulin</code></h2>\n<p>CreateInsulinDose</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-InsulinDose\">InsulinDose</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>201</td><td>A dose</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-InsulinDose\">InsulinDose</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"GetInsulinDose\">\n<h2><code>GET /data/insulin/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>GetInsulinDose</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A dose</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-InsulinDose\">InsulinDose</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"UpdateInsulinDose\">\n<h2><code>POST /data/insulin/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>UpdateInsulinDose</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-InsulinDose\">InsulinDose</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>A dose</td><td>{result: <a href=\"#schema-InsulinDose\">InsulinDose</a>, status: integer}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"DeleteInsulinDose\">\n<h2><code>DELETE /data/insulin/{id}</code></h2>\n<p>DeleteInsulinDose</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (required)</td><td>path</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Deleted</td><td>{status: string}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"Login\">\n<h2><code>POST /login</code></h2>\n<p>Signs an admin (with TOTP) or user in, for a JWT</p>\n\n<p>No sign in needed</p>\n\n<h3>Body</h3><p><code>application/json</code>: <a href=\"#schema-LoginRequest\">LoginRequest</a></p>\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>Signed in</td><td><a href=\"#schema-LoginToken\">LoginToken</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"CreateSite\">\n<h2><code>POST /site</code></h2>\n<p>Creates a site, on the public host, and gives its credentials once</p>\n\n<p>No sign in needed</p>\n\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>The new site</td><td><a href=\"#schema-CreatedSite\">CreatedSite</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"GetSummary\">\n<h2><code>GET /summary</code></h2>\n<p>The site&#39;s summary over the last hours (48 by default, a week at most)</p>\n\n<p>Signed in with a JWT as Authorization: Bearer</p>\n<h3>Parameters</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>In</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>hours</code></td><td>query</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Responses</h3>\n<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Description</th><th>Body</th></tr>\n<tr><td>200</td><td>The summary, as a list of one</td><td><a href=\"#schema-SummaryList\">SummaryList</a></td></tr>\n<tr><td>default</td><td>An error</td><td><a href=\"#schema-Error\">Error</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<h2>Schemas</h2>\n\n<section id=\"schema-CleanGlucoseReading\">\n<h3>CleanGlucoseReading</h3>\n\n<p>Has every field of <a href=\"#schema-GlucoseReading\">GlucoseReading</a></p>\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>diff_per_5m</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>source</code></td><td>string</td><td>direct, or the sync that wrote it: nightscout, dexcom, libre or virtual</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-CreatedSite\">\n<h3>CreatedSite</h3>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>api_key</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td>The admin&#39;s password</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>backup_key</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td>Gets a new admin login on the recover page; it works once</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>pwd_nstoken</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td>The PWD phone&#39;s Nightscout token</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>read_only_nstoken</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td>The read only device&#39;s Nightscout token</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>site_subdomain</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>totp_secret</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td>The admin&#39;s TOTP secret</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-Error\">\n<h3>Error</h3>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>message</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>status</code></td><td>integer</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-FoodIntake\">\n<h3>FoodIntake</h3>\n\n<p>Has every field of <a href=\"#schema-Record\">Record</a></p>\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>absorption_time_minutes</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>carbs</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td>Grams</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>category</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>energy</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>fat</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>fibre</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>food_type</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>portions</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>pre_bolus</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>protein</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>subcategory</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-GlucoseReading\">\n<h3>GlucoseReading</h3>\n\n<p>Has every field of <a href=\"#schema-Record\">Record</a></p>\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>delta</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>direction</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>filtered</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>measurement_method</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>noise</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>original_units</code></td><td><a href=\"#schema-Units\">Units</a></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>reading</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td>In units</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>reading_type</code></td><td>string</td><td>sgv from a sensor or mbg from a meter</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>rssi</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>unfiltered</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>units</code></td><td><a href=\"#schema-Units\">Units</a></td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-InsulinDose\">\n<h3>InsulinDose</h3>\n\n<p>Has every field of <a href=\"#schema-Record\">Record</a></p>\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>dose</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td>Units of insulin</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>dose_type</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>split_ext</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>split_now</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-LoginRequest\">\n<h3>LoginRequest</h3>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>name</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>password</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>totp</code></td><td>string</td><td>A code from the authenticator app, for an admin</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-LoginToken\">\n<h3>LoginToken</h3>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>expires_at</code> (required)</td><td>string (date-time)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>token</code> (required)</td><td>string</td><td>A JWT, sent as `Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;`</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-NsAuthorization\">\n<h3>NsAuthorization</h3>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>exp</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>iat</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>permissionGroups</code></td><td>array of array of string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>sub</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>token</code></td><td>string</td><td>A JWT, sent as `Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;`</td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-NsDocument\">\n<h3>NsDocument</h3>\n<p>A Nightscout document, such as an entry or treatment; the fields named here are common to most, the rest are kept in AdditionalProperties</p>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>_id</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>carbs</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>created_at</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>date</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>dateString</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>device</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>direction</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>enteredBy</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>eventType</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>identifier</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>insulin</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>isValid</code></td><td>boolean</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>mbg</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td>In units</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>notes</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>sgv</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td>In units</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>srvCreated</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>srvModified</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>type</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>units</code></td><td>string</td><td>The units of sgv and mbg, the identity&#39;s</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>utcOffset</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-Record\">\n<h3>Record</h3>\n<p>What every record has. Read only fields are set by the server, which ignores them if sent.</p>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>created_at</code> (read only)</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>created_by_app_name</code> (read only)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>created_by_device_name</code> (read only)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>created_by_identity_name</code> (read only)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>id</code> (read only)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>notes</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>occurred_at</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td>Now, if not sent when creating</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>raw_json_data</code> (read only)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>reason</code></td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>updated_at</code> (read only)</td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>updated_by_identity_name</code> (read only)</td><td>string</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>utc_offset_minutes</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-Summary\">\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n<p>The parts of the summary described here; the rest is kept in AdditionalProperties</p>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>food_intakes</code></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-FoodIntake\">FoodIntake</a></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>glucose_readings</code></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-CleanGlucoseReading\">CleanGlucoseReading</a></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>hours</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>insulin_doses</code></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-InsulinDose\">InsulinDose</a></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>range_high</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>range_low</code></td><td>number (double)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>since</code></td><td>integer (int64)</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>units</code></td><td><a href=\"#schema-Units\">Units</a></td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-SummaryList\">\n<h3>SummaryList</h3>\n\n\n<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>result</code></td><td>array of <a href=\"#schema-Summary\">Summary</a></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>status</code></td><td>integer</td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"schema-Units\">\n<h3>Units</h3>\n\n\n<p>string, one of mg/dL, mmol/L</p>\n</section>\n\n"
